# M54 Execution Changes Log — Default User, RAG Ingestion & Tagged Logging

> **Milestone:** 54 — DB seed, RAG document ingestion and tagged logging
> **Prompt:** `PROMPT-BACKEND-DB-RAG-USER-54.txt`
> **Role:** @Coder (Clean Architecture, EF Core, structured logging)

## 1. Summary

Closed the RAG feature loop requested by prompt 54:

1. A default test user (`Id = 1`, `Name = 'Test User'`,
   `Email = 'test@nutriexercise.local'`) is guaranteed to exist on startup.
2. A new document ingestion endpoint `POST /api/rag/ingest` accepts
   `Title`, `Content` and `BodyZone`, generates an embedding, stores it through
   pgvector and associates the row with the default test user.
3. Both `/api/rag/query` and `/api/rag/ingest` resolve to `UserId = 1` when no
   explicit `UserId`/auth token is supplied.
4. All RAG events are emitted through `IRagLogger` with the explicit
   `[RAG-INFO]:` / `[RAG-ERROR]:` prefixes.
5. Code is production-ready: DI-complete, analyzer-clean and covered by tests.

## 2. Baseline state found

The working tree already contained the pieces delivered by prompts 50/51:

- `DefaultUser`, `IUserRepository`/`UserRepository.EnsureSeedUserAsync` and
  `DbInitializer.InitializeAsync` (seeded the default user and ran migrations).
- `RagLogger` emitting `[RAG-INFO]:` / `[RAG-ERROR]:` through
  `ILogger<RagLogger>`.
- `RealRagOrchestrator` / `MockRagOrchestrator` behind the `UseMockMode` toggle,
  plus `POST /api/rag/query` with default-user resolution.

Gaps addressed here:

- `ResearchDocument` had **no ownership or body-zone fields**, so ingestion could
  not associate a document with the user or classify it by body zone.
- There was **no `/api/rag/ingest` endpoint** on `RagController`; the only
  ingestion path was `KnowledgeController` and it discarded the resolved user.
- `IRagOrchestrator` only exposed `ExecuteQueryAsync`.

## 3. Files modified

### `NutriExercise.Core/Entities/ResearchDocument.cs`
Added `string BodyZone` (default `string.Empty`) and `int UserId` so documents
carry their anatomical region and owner.

### `NutriExercise.Core/DTOs/RagContracts.cs`
Added the ingestion contract:

```csharp
public record RagIngestRequest(
    string Title,
    string Content,
    string BodyZone,
    int? UserId = null);

public record RagIngestResponse(
    Guid Id,
    string Title,
    string BodyZone,
    int UserId,
    int Dimensions,
    string Message);
```

`UserId` is optional in the request so the controller can fall back to the
default user when no authentication token is present.

### `NutriExercise.Core/Interfaces/IRagOrchestrator.cs`
Added `IngestAsync(RagIngestRequest, int userId, CancellationToken)` so the
mock/real strategy toggle governs ingestion as well as querying.

### `NutriExercise.Infrastructure/Services/RealRagOrchestrator.cs`
- Injects `IAiService` (embeddings) and `IResearchDocumentRepository` (persistence).
- `IngestAsync` generates the embedding, rejects empty embeddings with an
  `InvalidOperationException`, builds a `ResearchDocument` owned by `userId`
  with the supplied `BodyZone`, persists it, and logs the successful insertion:

  ```
  [RAG-INFO]: Vector inserted. DocumentId=…, UserId=…, BodyZone=…, Dimensions=…
  ```

  Failures (e.g. pgvector/DB exceptions) are logged via
  `[RAG-ERROR]: Document ingestion failed. …` and rethrown so the global
  exception middleware returns a 500.

### `NutriExercise.Infrastructure/Services/MockRagOrchestrator.cs`
Added the offline `IngestAsync` counterpart returning a deterministic
`RagIngestResponse` and an informational log, keeping the toggle symmetrical.

### `NutriExercise.Api/Controllers/RagController.cs`
Added `POST /api/rag/ingest`:

- Validates `Title`, `Content` and `BodyZone` (400 when any is blank).
- Resolves the effective user via the shared `ResolveUserIdAsync` helper
  (existing user when a valid `UserId` is supplied, otherwise the seeded
  default user `Id = 1`).
- Delegates to `IRagOrchestrator.IngestAsync` and logs the endpoint completion
  with `[RAG-INFO]:`.

### `NutriExercise.Api/Controllers/KnowledgeController.cs`
Both the single-document and bulk-seed paths now persist `UserId = <resolved>`
and `BodyZone = "General"` instead of discarding the resolved user.

## 4. Database migration

`dotnet ef migrations add AddDocumentOwnershipAndBodyZone` produced
`20260921144114_AddDocumentOwnershipAndBodyZone`:

- `ResearchDocuments.BodyZone` (`text`, not null, default `''`).
- `ResearchDocuments.UserId` (`integer`, not null, default `0`).
- A backfill `UPDATE "ResearchDocuments" SET "UserId" = 1 WHERE "UserId" = 0;`
  so documents seeded before this milestone are owned by the default user.

The model snapshot was regenerated automatically.

## 5. Tests

Added to `NutriExercise.Tests`:

- `RagControllerTests` — valid ingest delegates to the orchestrator and returns
  200; missing `UserId` associates the default test user; explicit `UserId`
  uses the existing user and never seeds; blank `Title`/`Content`/`BodyZone`
  returns 400 without touching the orchestrator; success logs `[RAG-INFO]`.
- `RealRagOrchestratorTests` — ingest embeds and persists an owned document,
  empty embeddings log `[RAG-ERROR]` and skip persistence, null request throws.
- `MockRagOrchestratorTests` — mock ingest returns the resolved user and a
  non-empty document id; null request throws.

